
---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Recovery & Rest | Silken Valley Lifestyle"
  description="Explore rest days, sleep habits, active recovery, relaxation, hydration, and healthy routines that support an active lifestyle."
  heroTitle="Recovery & Rest"
  heroText="Balance exercise with rest, relaxation, and everyday habits that support your overall well-being."
  heroCompact={true}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Fitness & Active Living</p>
    <h1>Recovery, Rest & Everyday Wellness</h1>
    <p>
      A balanced fitness routine is about more than exercise.
      Rest, sleep, hydration, nutrition, and relaxation all
      contribute to maintaining an active lifestyle.
      Discover practical ways to make recovery an important
      part of your everyday routine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="recovery-intro">
    <h2>Why Recovery Matters</h2>
    <p>
      Exercise places demands on the body, making recovery
      an important part of a sustainable fitness programme.
      Rest days and good sleep habits allow time for the body
      to adapt to physical activity. A balanced approach
      combines movement with sufficient rest and attention
      to how you feel.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="recovery-grid">
    <article class="recovery-card">
      <span class="recovery-number">01</span>
      <h2>Rest Days</h2>
      <p>
        Rest days provide a break from structured exercise
        and help prevent your weekly routine from becoming
        overwhelming.
      </p>
      <h3>Rest Day Ideas</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Take a break from strenuous exercise.</li>
        <li>Enjoy a relaxed walk if it feels comfortable.</li>
        <li>Spend time reading or enjoying a hobby.</li>
        <li>Prioritize a regular bedtime.</li>
        <li>Allow time for relaxation and recreation.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="recovery-card">
      <span class="recovery-number">02</span>
      <h2>Sleep & Restful Nights</h2>
      <p>
        Quality sleep is an important part of physical
        recovery, energy, and general well-being.
        Consistent habits can help support restful nights.
      </p>
      <h3>Healthy Sleep Habits</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Maintain a consistent sleep schedule.</li>
        <li>Create a comfortable sleeping environment.</li>
        <li>Develop a relaxing evening routine.</li>
        <li>Reduce screen use before bedtime.</li>
        <li>Keep your bedroom quiet and comfortable.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="recovery-card">
      <span class="recovery-number">03</span>
      <h2>Active Recovery</h2>
      <p>
        Active recovery involves gentle movement on
        lighter training days. It offers an alternative
        to complete rest when comfortable movement
        feels beneficial.
      </p>
      <h3>Activities to Explore</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Easy neighbourhood walks.</li>
        <li>Gentle cycling.</li>
        <li>Relaxed swimming.</li>
        <li>Light stretching.</li>
        <li>Gentle mobility exercises.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="recovery-card">
      <span class="recovery-number">04</span>
      <h2>Hydration & Nutrition</h2>
      <p>
        Drinking enough fluids and enjoying balanced meals
        are important everyday habits that support an
        active lifestyle.
      </p>
      <h3>Everyday Habits</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Drink water regularly throughout the day.</li>
        <li>Include a variety of fruits and vegetables.</li>
        <li>Enjoy protein-rich foods with meals.</li>
        <li>Include whole grains and nourishing foods.</li>
        <li>Adjust fluid intake to activity and conditions.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="recovery-card">
      <span class="recovery-number">05</span>
      <h2>Relaxation & Stress Management</h2>
      <p>
        Relaxation is an important part of overall
        well-being. Making time to slow down can help
        create a healthier balance between activity
        and everyday responsibilities.
      </p>
      <h3>Relaxation Ideas</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Practise slow, comfortable breathing.</li>
        <li>Enjoy quiet time outdoors.</li>
        <li>Listen to calming music.</li>
        <li>Read or spend time on a favourite hobby.</li>
        <li>Include gentle stretching in your evening routine.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="recovery-card">
      <span class="recovery-number">06</span>
      <h2>Listening to Your Body</h2>
      <p>
        Paying attention to changes in energy, comfort,
        and exercise performance can help you make
        sensible adjustments to your routine.
      </p>
      <h3>Things to Notice</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Unusual or persistent fatigue.</li>
        <li>Muscle soreness that does not improve.</li>
        <li>Changes in sleep quality.</li>
        <li>Reduced motivation or performance.</li>
        <li>Discomfort during everyday movement.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="recovery-routine">
    <p class="eyebrow">Planning & Balance</p>
    <h2>A Sample Weekly Recovery Routine</h2>
    <p>
      Recovery can be included throughout the week rather
      than reserved for one particular day. This example
      combines exercise with rest and lighter activities.
    </p>

    <div class="recovery-table">
      <div class="recovery-row">
        <strong>Monday</strong>
        <span>Exercise followed by a gentle cool-down</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recovery-row">
        <strong>Tuesday</strong>
        <span>Regular hydration and a consistent bedtime</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recovery-row">
        <strong>Wednesday</strong>
        <span>Gentle walking or active recovery</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recovery-row">
        <strong>Thursday</strong>
        <span>Stretching and relaxation</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recovery-row">
        <strong>Friday</strong>
        <span>Balanced meals and restful sleep</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recovery-row">
        <strong>Saturday</strong>
        <span>Enjoyable recreational movement</span>
      </div>
      <div class="recovery-row">
        <strong>Sunday</strong>
        <span>Rest, recharge, and prepare for the week</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="recovery-note">
    <h2>Build a Balanced Lifestyle</h2>
    <p>
      A healthy routine should leave room for both activity
      and rest. Avoid treating recovery as something you
      have to earn. Take additional rest when needed,
      maintain regular sleep habits, and make time for
      activities that help you unwind. If you experience
      persistent pain, unusual exhaustion, or other
      concerning symptoms, seek advice from a qualified
      health professional.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="recovery-links">
    <h2>Explore More Fitness Activities</h2>
    <div class="recovery-link-grid">
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/">Workouts & Exercise Routines →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/walking/">Walking & Cardio →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/stretching/">Stretching & Flexibility →</a>
      <a href="/fitness/workouts/low-impact/">Low-Impact Exercise →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="recovery-back">
    <a href="/fitness/">← Return to Fitness</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .recovery-intro {
    margin: 30px 0;
    padding: 28px;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .recovery-intro h2,
  .recovery-routine h2,
  .recovery-note h2,
  .recovery-links h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.7rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .recovery-intro p,
  .recovery-routine > p:not(.eyebrow),
  .recovery-note p {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .recovery-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin: 35px 0;
  }

  .recovery-card {
    padding: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .recovery-number {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .recovery-card h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 0 0 13px;
  }

  .recovery-card h3 {
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    margin: 22px 0 10px;
  }

  .recovery-card p,
  .recovery-card li {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .recovery-card p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .recovery-card ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .recovery-routine {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }

  .recovery-routine .eyebrow {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .recovery-table {
    margin-top: 22px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .recovery-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr;
    gap: 15px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
  }

  .recovery-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .recovery-row strong {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
  }

  .recovery-row span {
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .recovery-note {
    padding: 30px;
    margin: 40px 0;
    background: var(--rose-wash);
    border-radius: 18px;
  }

  .recovery-links {
    margin: 40px 0;
  }

  .recovery-link-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 15px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }

  .recovery-link-grid a {
    display: block;
    padding: 18px;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .recovery-link-grid a:hover {
    background: var(--rose-wash);
  }

  .recovery-back {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .recovery-back a {
    color: var(--accent-dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .recovery-back a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .recovery-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .recovery-link-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .recovery-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 5px;
    }
  }
</style>
